// ST7789/ILI9341 setup, RGB444. {rs, byte}: rs=0 command, rs=1 parameter.
// Identical to setup_st7789_565.hex except for COLMOD, and it exists as a
// second file rather than a parameter because the init sequence is a ROM the
// synthesis tools load with $readmemh - there is nowhere to put a conditional.
//
//   0_3A 1_03  COLMOD 12 bits/pixel. 1_05 is the 16-bit mode; the difference on
//              the wire is THREE BYTES PER TWO PIXELS instead of two per one,
//              so sending this file while rtl/lcd.sv is built for RGBSIZE=16
//              (or the reverse) does not discolour the image, it shears it -
//              the panel unpacks a 480-byte line as 320 pixels or a 640-byte
//              line as 426. rtl/lcd.sv's INIT_FILE parameter is what keeps the
//              two in step.
//
// Everything else is as measured on the MuseLab PMOD-TFTLCD; see the 565 file
// for why INVOFF and MADCTL 0xE8 are what they are.
0_20
0_2A 1_00 1_00 1_01 1_3F
0_2B 1_00 1_00 1_00 1_EF
0_3A 1_03
0_36 1_E8
0_29
